Chapter: BrowserEvent
  cites UI chapter Event
  cites UI chapter KeyInput
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Browser-level event routing. Maps raw keyboard and mouse events
 to browser actions. Keyboard shortcuts follow standard browser
 conventions adapted for Codex.

Section: Types

  BrowserAction =
    | ActionNone
    | ActionNewTab
    | ActionCloseTab
    | ActionFocusAddress
    | ActionReload
    | ActionBack
    | ActionForward
    | ActionNextTab
    | ActionPrevTab
    | ActionStop
    | ActionNavigate (Text)
    | ActionSwitchTab (Integer)
    | ActionAddressKey (Event)
    | ActionPageEvent (Event)
    | ActionScrollUp
    | ActionScrollDown
    | ActionPageUp
    | ActionPageDown
    | ActionHome
    | ActionEnd

Section: Modifier Constants

  mod-shift : Integer
  mod-shift = 1

  mod-ctrl : Integer
  mod-ctrl = 2

  mod-alt : Integer
  mod-alt = 4

Section: Key Code Constants

 This chapter used to carry its own copy of the whole key table, in DOM
 codes, which is where `key-f5 = 116` came from and why plain `t` reloaded
 the page: 116 is also the letter. `UI chapter KeyInput` owns the named
 keys now, and a character is written as a character. There is one table.

Section: Key Mapping

  map-key-event : Event -> BrowserAction
  map-key-event (ev) =
    when ev.ev-kind
      is EvKeyDown (k) (mods) ->
        if has-mod mods mod-ctrl
        then map-ctrl-key k mods
        else if has-mod mods mod-alt
        then map-alt-key k
        else map-plain-key k
      is otherwise -> ActionNone

  has-mod : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  has-mod (mods) (flag) =
    int-mod (mods / flag) 2 == 1

  map-ctrl-key : Integer, Integer -> BrowserAction
  map-ctrl-key (k0) (mods) =
    let k = key-upper k0
    in if k == (char-code 'T') then ActionNewTab
    else if k == (char-code 'W') then ActionCloseTab
    else if k == (char-code 'L') then ActionFocusAddress
    else if k == (char-code 'R') then ActionReload
    else if k == key-tab then
      if has-mod mods mod-shift
      then ActionPrevTab
      else ActionNextTab
    else ActionNone

  map-alt-key : Integer -> BrowserAction
  map-alt-key (k) =
    if k == key-left then ActionBack
    else if k == key-right then ActionForward
    else ActionNone

  map-plain-key : Integer -> BrowserAction
  map-plain-key (k) =
    if k == key-f5 then ActionReload
    else if k == key-escape then ActionStop
    else if k == key-up then ActionScrollUp
    else if k == key-down then ActionScrollDown
    else if k == key-pgup then ActionPageUp
    else if k == key-pgdn then ActionPageDown
    else if k == key-home then ActionHome
    else if k == key-end then ActionEnd
    else ActionNone

Section: Event Polling

 In the bare-metal environment, events come from the keyboard
 service (poll-key) and the kernel mouse module. poll-key
 returns a canonical key code as an Integer, or 0 if no key is
 pending, and `poll-mods` the held shift/ctrl/alt at that moment
 (the same bit values `mod-shift`/`mod-ctrl`/`mod-alt` above use).
 A letter is case-sensitive, so `map-ctrl-key` folds it through
 `key-upper` before matching a shortcut; the nav and function keys
 are DOM key codes used unchanged.

 For the MVP, we poll the keyboard. Mouse support requires the
 kernel Mouse module (PS/2 or USB HID).

  browser-poll-event : [Console] Event
  browser-poll-event = act
    let key-code = poll-key
    in if key-code == 0
      then event-timer "tick" 0
      else event-key-down key-code poll-mods 0
  end

Section: Event Classification

  is-navigation-action : BrowserAction -> Boolean
  is-navigation-action (action) =
    when action
      is ActionBack -> True
      is ActionForward -> True
      is ActionReload -> True
      is ActionNavigate (_) -> True
      is otherwise -> False

  is-tab-action : BrowserAction -> Boolean
  is-tab-action (action) =
    when action
      is ActionNewTab -> True
      is ActionCloseTab -> True
      is ActionNextTab -> True
      is ActionPrevTab -> True
      is ActionSwitchTab (_) -> True
      is otherwise -> False

  action-name : BrowserAction -> Text
  action-name (action) =
    when action
      is ActionNone -> "none"
      is ActionNewTab -> "new-tab"
      is ActionCloseTab -> "close-tab"
      is ActionFocusAddress -> "focus-address"
      is ActionReload -> "reload"
      is ActionBack -> "back"
      is ActionForward -> "forward"
      is ActionNextTab -> "next-tab"
      is ActionPrevTab -> "prev-tab"
      is ActionStop -> "stop"
      is ActionNavigate (addr) -> "navigate:" & addr
      is ActionSwitchTab (id) -> "switch-tab:" & show id
      is ActionAddressKey (_) -> "address-key"
      is ActionPageEvent (_) -> "page-event"
      is ActionScrollUp -> "scroll-up"
      is ActionScrollDown -> "scroll-down"
      is ActionPageUp -> "page-up"
      is ActionPageDown -> "page-down"
      is ActionHome -> "home"
      is ActionEnd -> "end"
